# Copy to .env and fill in keys (never commit .env).

# --- NVIDIA NIM (OpenAI-compatible) ---
# Connection (models API + chat): list models works with the key alone.
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-...
# HZ_API_KEY=nvapi-...          # same value; hzcode reads HZ_API_KEY for registry hosts
# HZ_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com
# HZ_PROVIDER=openai          # built-in openai adapter against NIM (no trailing /v1)
# HZ_MODEL=minimaxai/minimax-m3.1-flash   # example deployed on some keys (2026-11-11 README row); must be non-EOL and deployed for your account
# Optional live chat test (uses HZ_NVIDIA_CHAT_MODEL or minimaxai/minimax-m3.1-flash, not HZ_MODEL):
# HZ_NVIDIA_CHAT_PROBE=1 bun test tests/providers/nvidia-live.test.ts
# HZ_NVIDIA_CHAT_MODEL=minimaxai/minimax-m3.1-flash

# TUI /models for NIM catalog ids: add a user config provider id `nvidia` (see docs/15 §3.1)
# or set HZ_PROVIDER=nvidia with a matching `providers[]` entry in ~/.config/horizon/config.json.

# Smoke (with .env): bash ops/nvidia-smoke.sh
# Tests: NVIDIA_API_KEY=… bun test app/tests/providers/nvidia-live.test.ts
